    "accession": "PXD015682",
    "title": "Characterization of Integrator module INTS10-INTS13-INTS14 and its connection to the cleavage module Part I",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Chemical cross-linking coupled to mass spectrometry was used to study the complex between the Integrator complex subunits INTS13 (Asunder) and INTS14. Cross-linking was performed using disuccinimidyl suberate (DSS).",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Chemical cross-linking was performed following previously described procedures (Leitner et al., Nat. Protoc., 2014). Samples were digested (1) with endoproteinase Lys-C followed by trypsin or (2) with endoproteinase Asp-N. Digests were fractionated by size-exclusion chromatography and SEC fractions were analyzed by data-dependent LC-MS/MS on a Thermo Orbitrap Fusion Lumos system.  Additional experimental details are provided in the accompanying publication.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "MS/MS spectra were searched using xQuest (Walzthoeni et al., Nat. Methods, 2012), version 2.1.4, against the sequences of target proteins and identified contaminants.   Additional search settings were as follows: Enzyme = trypsin or Asp-N, maximum number of missed cleavages = 2, MS mass tolerances dependent on the respective data set, MS/MS mass tolerance = 0.2 Da for “common”-type fragment ions and 0.3 Da for “xlink”-type fragment ions. The original scoring scheme of xQuest (Rinner et al., Nat. Methods, 2008) was used.  All cross-linking identifications are compiled in a spreadsheet file in Microsoft Excel format. A separate spreadsheet connects the raw files and the individual cross-linking experiments and SEC fractions.",
